    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The primary on\u2011call engineer for the checkout\u2011api service is **Nabil\u202fFerhat**\u3010ONC-PAY#0.0\u3011\u3010SVC-CHECKOUT#0.0\u3011.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M02",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.5,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "**Runbook that applies:**  \n- **RB\u2011PAY\u2011DECLINES** \u2013 \u201cCard payment declines spike\u201d [RB-PAY-DECLINES#3.0].\n\n**Escalation contact:**  \n- Page the **Checkout & Payments escalation contact** (as stated in the runbook\u2019s Escalate section) [RB-PAY-DECLINES#3.0].",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 0.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M03",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.3333333333333333,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "Page the primary on\u2011call for TEAM\u2011PLATFORM first: **Kamel\u202fBenyahia** (primary on\u2011call for the Platform rota). If no response within 5\u202fminutes, page the secondary, Meriem\u202fAit\u202fAhmed.  \n[ONC-PLATFORM#1.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M04",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The services that depend directly on **redis\u2011cache** are:\n\n- **auth-service** (ID\u202f`SVC-AUTH`) \u2013 uses Redis for session caching\u202f[SVC-AUTH#0.0]  \n- **storefront-web** (ID\u202f`SVC-STOREFRONT`) \u2013 uses Redis for page caching\u202f[SVC-STOREFRONT#0.0]  \n- **checkout-api** (ID\u202f`SVC-CHECKOUT`) \u2013 uses Redis for cart storage\u202f[SVC-CHECKOUT#0.0]  \n\nGraph paths confirm the dependencies:  \n`SVC-REDIS <-[DEPENDS_ON]- SVC-AUTH`, `SVC-REDIS <-[DEPENDS_ON]- SVC-STOREFRONT`, `SVC-REDIS <-[DEPENDS_ON]- SVC-CHECKOUT`.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M05",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "If the primary database (SVC\u2011MAINDB) goes down, any service that depends on it cannot function:\n\n* **Orders\u2011service** \u2013 stores orders in the orders schema; without the DB it cannot write or read orders, causing order failures and connection\u2011pool exhaustion. [SVC-ORDERS#0.0] [SVC-ORDERS#2.0]  \n* **Payments\u2011gateway** \u2013 records payment data in main\u2011db; without it payment records cannot be written and the service will time\u2011out. [SVC-PAYMENTS#0.0] [SVC-PAYMENTS#2.0]  \n* **Catalog\u2011service** \u2013 keeps product data in the catalog schema; without the DB it cannot serve product pages. [SVC-CATALOG#0.0] [SVC-CATALOG#2.0]  \n* **Auth\u2011service** \u2013 stores user accounts in main\u2011db; without it no user can sign in. [SVC-AUTH#0.0] [SVC-AUTH#2.0]  \n\nOther services that reference main\u2011db (not listed here) would also be affected.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M06",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.5,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The outage was caused by the Redis service (SVC\u2011REDIS).  \nThat service is owned by **Team Platform** (TEAM\u2011PLATFORM)\u3010ADR-002#3.0\u3011\u3010ADR-002 -[APPLIES_TO]-> SVC-REDIS -[OWNED_BY]-> TEAM-PLATFORM\u3011.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M07",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "After the August\u202f2025 card\u2011payment outage, the team decided to **monitor and automate external certificates** and to add operational safeguards for future renewals. Specifically, TEAM\u2011PAY will:\n\n* add an alert 30\u202fdays before any external certificate expires by\u202f2025\u201108\u201131, and  \n* add a feature flag to switch checkout to cash\u2011on\u2011delivery only by\u202f2025\u201108\u201120.  \n\nThese actions are documented in the post\u2011mortem and the ADR\u2011003 decision [PM-2025-08#3.0][ADR-003#1.0].",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M08",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The old Redis restart runbook (RB\u2011REDIS\u2011RESTART) was replaced by **RB\u2011REDIS\u2011FAILOVER**\u202f[RB\u2011REDIS\u2011RESTART#0.0].  \nIn the new runbook it explicitly states: **\u201cNever restart the primary while it is the only healthy node.\u201d**\u202f[RB\u2011REDIS\u2011FAILOVER#2.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M09",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "ADR\u2011002 superseded ADR\u2011001 [ADR-001#0.0][ADR-002#0.0].  \nRedis now runs as a primary with one replica and Redis Sentinel; the replica is automatically promoted if the primary fails [SVC-REDIS#1.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M10",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The team that owns **search\u2011api** is **Search & Catalog** (TEAM\u2011DISCOVERY).  \nIts lead is **Imene Djebbar**\u3010TEAM-DISCOVERY#0.0\u3011.  \nThe ownership link is shown by the graph path **SVC\u2011SEARCH \u2192 OWNED_BY \u2192 TEAM\u2011DISCOVERY**\u3010SVC-SEARCH -[OWNED_BY]-> TEAM-DISCOVERY\u3011.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M11",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "Yes \u2013 the events\u2011bus (SVC\u2011EVENTS) was the root cause of the 2025\u201106 incident that delayed SMS by up to 9\u202fhours [PM-2025-06#0.0].  The follow\u2011up runbook created to address the backlog is **RB\u2011EVENTS\u2011BACKLOG** [RB-EVENTS-BACKLOG#0.0].",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M12",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The notifications\u2011worker is owned by **TEAM\u2011ORDERS**.  \nThe on\u2011call rota for that team is:\n\n* **Primary:** Sara\u202fMeziane  \n* **Secondary:** Hamza\u202fToumi  \n* **Escalation:** Rachid\u202fBouzid  \n\n[SVC\u2011NOTIFY#0.0] \u2192 [ONC\u2011ORDERS#0.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M13",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.6666666666666666,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The Platform team received two action items from the postmortems:\n\n1. Add a dead\u2011letter queue to every queue on the events bus by\u202f2025\u201107\u201115.\u202f[PM-2025-06#3.0]  \n2. Run Redis with a replica and Sentinel by\u202f2025\u201104\u201130.\u202f[PM-2025-03#3.0]",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M14",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.5,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The Numidia\u202fPay client\u2011certificate expiry caused a failure in the **payments\u2011gateway** service (SVC\u2011PAYMENTS) \u2013 all card payments were refused for 2\u202fh\u202f10\u202fm until the certificate was renewed. Cash\u2011on\u2011delivery orders continued to work normally. [PM-2025-08#1.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M15",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "Checkout\u2011API depends on the payments\u2011gateway, which in turn calls the external provider **SVC\u2011NUMIDIAPAY** for card payments.  \nThe certificate alert for Numidia Pay, **NumidiaPayCertificateExpiry**, fires **30\u202fdays before the certificate expires**.  \n\n- Checkout\u2011API \u2192 payments\u2011gateway \u2192 **SVC\u2011NUMIDIAPAY** [SVC-CHECKOUT#0.0][SVC-PAYMENTS#0.0]  \n- Certificate alert timing: 30\u202fdays before expiry [SVC-NUMIDIAPAY#3.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M16",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The orders\u2011service holds a pool of **40 database connections**\u202f[SVC-ORDERS#2.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M17",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The secondary on\u2011call for the team that owns **payments\u2011gateway** is **Lina Cherif** [ONC-PAY#0.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M18",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The only architecture decision that applies to **orders\u2011service** is:\n\n- **ADR\u2011004 \u2013 PgBouncer in front of main\u2011db** (orders\u2011service gets a fixed pool of 40 connections)\u3010ADR-004#2.0\u3011",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M19",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.3333333333333333,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 0.3333333333333333,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The cart\u2011loss issue is covered by the **RB\u2011REDIS\u2011FAILOVER** runbook, which lists \u201cCarts disappear for customers\u201d as a symptom.  \nThe root cause is the Redis service, which is owned by the **Platform** team.  \n\n- Runbook: **RB\u2011REDIS\u2011FAILOVER** [RB-REDIS-FAILOVER#1.0]  \n- Owner team: **TEAM\u2011PLATFORM** [TEAM-PLATFORM#2.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M20",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The June\u202f2025 events\u2011bus incident broke the message flow for every service that consumes events from the bus.  \nAffected services (directly or indirectly) were:\n\n* **notifications\u2011worker** \u2013 its SMS queue grew and triggered the\u202fSmsQueueBacklog alert [SVC\u2011NOTIFY#2.0].  \n* **orders\u2011service** \u2013 its order events were delayed, causing downstream lag [SVC\u2011ORDERS#1.0].  \n* **delivery\u2011tracker** \u2013 status updates fell behind, firing DeliveryStatusLag [SVC\u2011DELIVERY#2.0].  \n* **payments\u2011gateway** \u2013 payment events stalled, raising PaymentTimeouts [SVC\u2011PAYMENTS#2.0].  \n* **catalog\u2011service** \u2013 product\u2011change events were queued, leading to stale catalog data [SVC\u2011CATALOG#2.0].  \n* **search\u2011api** \u2013 product\u2011change events were delayed, making the index stale [SVC\u2011SEARCH#2.0].\n\nThe runbook for the backlog shows that the **SmsQueueBacklog** alert fires when more than **20,000** SMS messages are waiting in the queue [SVC\u2011NOTIFY#2.0]. Thus, over 20,000 SMS messages piled up during the incident.",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 0.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M21",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The database that catalog-service depends on is **SVC\u2011MAINDB**.  \nIts on\u2011call rota is **ONC\u2011PLATFORM**, whose escalation contact is **Sofiane Larbi**.  \n[ONC\u2011PLATFORM#0.0] [SVC\u2011MAINDB#0.0] [SVC\u2011CATALOG#0.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M22",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The Ramadan\u2011sale outage led to **ADR\u2011002 \u2013 \u201cDecision: Redis with a replica and Sentinel\u201d** being adopted, replacing the earlier single\u2011host approach.  \nThe runbook specifies that a failover should complete in **under 30\u202fseconds**. [ADR\u2011002#2.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M23",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The storefront\u2011web service depends on **SVC\u2011CHECKOUT** for buying, and that service is owned by the Checkout & Payments team (TEAM\u2011PAY) [SVC-STOREFRONT#0.0][SVC-CHECKOUT#0.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   }
  ]
 },
